---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://packagingconveyor.com/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": "https://packagingconveyor.com/about/" }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About PackagingConveyor.com | Independent Conveyor Technical Resource"
  description="PackagingConveyor.com is an independent, vendor-neutral technical resource on packaging conveyors for plant engineers and packaging managers."
  canonical="https://packagingconveyor.com/about/"
  schema={[breadcrumbSchema]}
>
<h1>About This Resource</h1>
<h2 id="what-heading">Independent. Vendor-Neutral.</h2>
<p><strong>PackagingConveyor.com is not a manufacturer. It is not a distributor.</strong> We do not sell equipment, take commissions, or represent any conveyor brand.</p>
<p>This is an independent editorial resource: vendor-neutral technical guides for plant engineers, packaging managers, and capital project teams who need reliable data to specify conveyor systems.</p>
<p>We cover <strong>30+ conveyor types</strong> across food and beverage, pharmaceutical, automotive, and warehouse applications. Every guide includes engineering specifications, selection criteria, and comparison data.</p>
<h2 id="audience-heading">Built for Engineers</h2>
<p>This site is built for people who design, specify, purchase, or maintain conveyor systems in packaging operations:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Plant engineers</strong> evaluating conveyor types for new lines or retrofits</li>
<li><strong>Packaging managers</strong> comparing system options across vendors</li>
<li><strong>Capital project teams</strong> building specifications and RFQ packages</li>
<li><strong>Maintenance engineers</strong> troubleshooting or planning replacements</li>
<li><strong>Procurement teams</strong> who need to understand what they are buying</li>
</ul>
<p>The content assumes you have working knowledge of packaging operations. We explain conveyor technology, not what a conveyor is.</p>
<h2 id="editorial-heading">How We Research</h2>
<p>Content on this site draws from manufacturer specification sheets, <a href="https://www.cema.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CEMA (Conveyor Equipment Manufacturers Association)</a> standards, <a href="https://www.asme.org/codes-standards/find-codes-standards/b20-1-safety-standard-conveyors-related-equipment" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ANSI/ASME B20.1</a> safety standards, FDA and USDA regulatory guidance, and direct industry experience in packaging line design and integration.</p>
<p><strong>Our editorial rules:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>We do not publish specific dollar pricing. Cost factors and relative comparisons only.</li>
<li>We do not accept payment for coverage, rankings, or recommendations.</li>
<li>We do not claim to test or certify equipment. We aggregate publicly available technical data.</li>
<li>We verify manufacturer names, parent companies, and product claims before publishing.</li>
<li>When data is uncertain, we flag it internally and use qualified language.</li>
</ul>
<p>If a conveyor type is covered here, it is because it is relevant to packaging operations, not because a manufacturer paid to be included.</p>
<h2 id="use-heading">What You Can Do Here</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="/conveyor-types/">Compare conveyor types</a> with technical specifications and selection criteria</li>
<li><a href="/industries/">Find industry-specific guides</a> for food, pharma, automotive, and warehouse conveyors</li>
<li><a href="/conveyor-functions/">Understand conveyor functions</a> like accumulation, singulation, indexing, and reject systems</li>
<li><a href="/resources/conveyor-design-guide/">Use engineering references</a> for <a href="/resources/conveyor-design-guide/conveyor-engineering/">belt pull calculations</a>, motor sizing, and throughput formulas</li>
<li><a href="/resources/conveyor-cost-guide/">Understand cost factors</a> that drive conveyor system budgets</li>
<li><a href="/resources/conveyor-manufacturers/">Research manufacturers</a> by conveyor type and capability</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="contact-heading">Get in Touch</h2>
<p>For editorial inquiries, corrections, or content feedback: <a href="mailto:info@packagingconveyor.com">info@packagingconveyor.com</a>.</p>
<p>We welcome corrections from industry professionals. If you see inaccurate technical data, outdated manufacturer information, or missing conveyor types, let us know.</p>
</BaseLayout>
